Wimbledon Begins, Ashleigh Barty Is on Top of the World', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Barty’s Rocket Ride Up the Rankings Hits No. 1 in Time for Wimbledon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barty, Ashleigh', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-01T05:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc149cda-5a49-5e5f-a3dd-4b0843a6399f', 'word_count': 894, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc149cda-5a49-5e5f-a3dd-4b0843a6399f'}, {'abstract': 'Sarah Jessica Parker’s comedy series returns for a fourth season. And the original “Veronica Mars” lands on Hulu ahead of a reboot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/01/arts/television/whats-on-tv-monday-divorce-and-veronica-mars.html', 'snippet': 'Sarah Jessica Parker’s comedy series returns for a fourth season. And the original “Veronica Mars” lands on Hulu ahead of a reboot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DIVORCE 10 p.m. on HBO; stream on HBO platforms. When this pitch-black comedy about the aftermath of a messy divorce debuted in 2016, critics gave it mixed reviews. Some found it too painful to enjoy, and the characters weren’t exactly a likable bunch. But its second season showed signs of improvement, mostly because we saw better sides of Frances (Sarah Jessica Parker) and Robert (Thomas Haden Church) as they moved on to different partners. In Season 3 (spoiler alert!), tensions rise as Robert’s wedding draws closer and he and Frances butt heads over their parenting styles. On the sidelines, Diane (Molly Shannon) searches for independence while her husband sits in prison, and Dallas (Talia Balsam) wrestles with a midlife crisis. Writing in The New York Times, James Poniewozik said the show isn’t “going to reinvent the breakup comedy or the HBO comedy. Its goal is more modest and midlife-appropriate: to tell one more story of two people trying to reinvent themselves.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/01/arts/01tvcol-divorce/265fd8e1aa1640deb75f6f03bd67c6b8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/01/arts/01tvcol-divorce/265fd8e1aa1640deb75f6f03bd67c6b8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/01/arts/01tvcol-divorce/265fd8e1aa1640deb75f6f03bd67c6b8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/01/arts/01tvcol-divorce/265fd8e1aa1640deb75f6f03bd67c6b8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/01/arts/01tvcol-divorce/01tvcol-divorce-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/01/arts/01tvcol-divorce/01tvcol-divorce-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image