ash Over Civil Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Kamala D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-01T19:30:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3e13c46-e166-51a7-8bf3-86a453b4fd2b', 'word_count': 457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3e13c46-e166-51a7-8bf3-86a453b4fd2b'}, {'abstract': 'The chef Marcus Samuelsson has a new audio cookbook that incorporates Harlem and his restaurant Red Rooster.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/01/dining/our-harlem-audible-marcus-samuelsson.html', 'snippet': 'The chef Marcus Samuelsson has a new audio cookbook that incorporates Harlem and his restaurant Red Rooster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Take Marcus Samuelsson along with you into the kitchen or even on the subway. The chef and restaurateur, who is based in Harlem, has a new audio cookbook that incorporates the neighborhood and his flagship restaurant, Red Rooster Harlem, with stops in your home kitchen to whip up some peanut-bacon pork chops, fish in banana leaves and a Bloody Rooster cocktail. Mr. Samuelsson teams up with personalities like the writers Jelani Cobb and Dr. Jessica B. Harris to cook, with jazz and gospel in the background. The narrative covers the history of Harlem and changes in the area: “It gives people a new way to experience the community,” Mr. Samuelsson said. It comes with a digital copy of the recipes. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01Burner8/merlin_107911852_65d4e1d0-0365-4171-b802-d8a25ad8b621-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01Burner8/merlin_107911852_65d4e1d0-0365-4171-b802-d8a25ad8b621-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01Burner8/merlin_107911852_65d4e1d0-0365-4171-b802-d8a25ad8b621-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01Burner8/merlin_107911852_65d4e1d0-0365-4171-b802-d8a25ad8b621-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01Burner8/01Burner8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01Burner8/01Burner8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01Burner8/01Burner8-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sound and Flavor Made in Harlem', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Listen: Sound and Flavor Made in Harlem', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Red Rooster (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samuelsson, Marcus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Audible.com', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-01T19:42:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63428721-4780-58e0-b1cd-b881bcd35884', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63428721-4780-58e0-b1cd-b881bcd35884'}, {'abstract': '“The Peach Truck Cookbook” has recipes for Dutch baby pancakes, cucumber gazpacho and pizza.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/01/dining/the-peach-truck-cookbook.html', 'snippet': '“The Peach Truck Cookbook” has recipes for Dutch baby pancakes, cucumber gazpacho and pizza.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stephen and Jessica Rose couldn’t find juicy, fragrant fresh peaches in Nashville, where they settled as newlyweds, so they did something about it. In 2012 the couple bought bushels of peaches — Mr. Rose is from Fort Valley, Ga., and was familiar with Pearson Farm there — loaded the fruit in a 1964 Jeep Gladiator and drove around Nashville selling them on weekends in summer. They are still at it with their peach truck, and visit more than 100 cities each summer. Now the couple has a cookbook that explains peach varieties, the history of the fruit in America and how to store, ripen and peel your peaches (though they don’t mention the serrated peeler I use for the job). Adding peaches to Dutch baby pancakes, to a cucumber gazpacho, to poundcake, to a Caprese salad and to condiments for pork and salmon are first-rate suggestions. I’m not sure I need peaches on pizza or with a steak, but when you’re in the peach business there are no limits. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner2/01burner2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 848, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner2/01burner2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 848}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner2/01burner2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 725, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner2/01burner2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1450, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner2/01burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner2/01burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner2/01burner2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Just Add Peaches', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Appreciate: Just Add Peaches To the Shopping List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Peaches', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Peach Truck Cookbook (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rose, Jessica N (1983- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rose, Stephen (1987- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-01T19:48:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbdaa398-762f-5e41-8e41-67fc023e06af', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbdaa398-762f-5e41-8e41-67fc023e06af'}, {'abstract': 'At Ironbound Farm in New Jersey, the owner built a giant steel grill for everyday and special meals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/01/dining/ironbound-farm-grill.html', 'snippet': 'At Ironbound Farm in New Jersey, the owner built a giant steel grill for everyday and special meals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before you fire up the Weber, you might want to take a trip to Ironbound Farm in Asbury, in Hunterdon County, N.J., where Charles Rosen, the owner, has completed construction of a monumental grill. Mr. Rosen calls it the “mother fire” and considers it the crowning touch at his farm, cidery, winery and tasting room. “I wanted to create a destination where chefs can cook,” he said. Mr. Rosen was inspired by Francis Mallmann, the Argentine chef known for grilling, and he worked with the metal designer Terrance Johnson and the chef Norberto Piattoni, who is from Argentina, to build the soaring, 26-foot-high sculptural steel grill. It’s now in use for burgers and sausages served in the tasting room, for whole pigs and yaks at parties open to the public and for special chef’s dinners, the next of which will be in early August with Mr. Piattoni cooking.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner3/merlin_156933480_07aef5cd-f2ae-4590-b16c-eb7b3bfc18fb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner3/merlin_156933480_07aef5cd-f2ae-4590-b16c-eb7b3bfc18fb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner3/merlin_156933480_07aef5cd-f2ae-4590-b16c-eb7b3bfc18fb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner3/merlin_156933480_07aef5cd-f2ae-4590-b16c-eb7b3bfc18fb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner3/merlin_156933480_07aef5cd-f2ae-4590-b16c-eb7b3bfc18fb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner3/merlin_156933480_07aef5cd-f2ae-4590-b16c-eb7b3bfc18fb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner3/merlin_156933480_07aef5cd-f2ae-4590-b16c-eb7b3bfc18fb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Grill Big Enough for a Yak', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Ignite: A Grill Big Enough To Handle a Yak', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grilling (Cooking)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jersey Cider Works', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hunterdon County (NJ)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-01T19:51:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea001180-b434-50a0-a9e0-e5043111b598', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea001180-b434-50a0-a9e0-e5043111b598'}, {'abstract': 'In a video, Ms. Grisham opens a path for American journalists to cover the president’s meeting with Kim Jong-un of North Korea. She has a bruise to show for it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/01/us/politics/stephanie-grisham-north-korea.html', 'snippet': 'In a video, Ms. Grisham opens a path for American journalists to cover the president’s meeting with Kim Jong-un of North Korea. She has a bruise to show for it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Stephanie Grisham, the new White House press secretary, returned from the Demilitarized Zone with a bruise on her arm after physically pushing North Korean officials to clear a way for American journalists to cover President Trump’s meeting with the North Korean leader, Kim Jong-un.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stephanie Grisham, Trump’s New Press Secretary, Literally Pushes for Press Access', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Press Secretary Makes a Literal, and Symbolic, Push for Access', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grisham, Stephanie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Sarah Huckabee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Korean Demilitarized Zone', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-01T19:51:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Karni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Karni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fda65101-e2bc-5a43-83c8-6e40fef486d9', 'word_count': 957, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fda65101-e2bc-5a43-83c8-6e40fef486d9'}, {'abstract': 'Satur Farms and Rick’s Picks have you covered for your next park excursion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/01/dining/satur-farms-salad-dressing-ricks-picks-pickles.html', 'snippet': 'Satur Farms and Rick’s Picks have you covered for your next park excursion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some picnic-worthy accouterments have just been introduced by familiar grocery store brands. After growing salad greens for over 20 years, Satur Farms, in Cutchogue, N.Y., has introduced vinaigrette-style dressings created by Eberhard Müller, an owner and a chef. Each of four varieties (spicy Asian, citrus, honey-balsamic and white truffle) comes in one-ounce single-portion packets, six to a container. They are all organic, made without preservatives and useful not just for a bowl of greens but to season seafood and grains. Also portable are single-serving packs of crisp pickle spears, the latest from Rick Field of Rick’s Picks in Brooklyn. Called “Snacking Pickles,” they come in five flavors — garlic-dill, sweet, sour, spicy Sriracha and cumin-lime-dill — in 2.2-ounce packs. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner7/01burner7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner7/01burner7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner7/01burner7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner7/01burner7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner7/01burner7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner7/01burner7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/dining/01burner7/01burner7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Picnic-Ready Dressings and Pickles', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Pac