', 'snippet': 'A new award aims to shine a light on a gender imbalance in photography.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Susan Meiselas, the much-lauded Magnum photographer perhaps best known for her arresting 1979 shot of a Nicaraguan revolutionary lobbing a Molotov cocktail, said she was caught by surprise when Sam Stourdzé, the director of the Rencontres d’Arles photography fair in France, phoned in April to say she had won a major new award — from a luxury fashion group.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/04/style/02KERING-PHOTOGRAPHER-new-girl/merlin_157294158_47449700-fad6-4b11-bc5a-f474bd8d3992-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/04/style/02KERING-PHOTOGRAPHER-new-girl/merlin_157294158_47449700-fad6-4b11-bc5a-f474bd8d3992-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/04/style/02KERING-PHOTOGRAPHER-new-girl/merlin_157294158_47449700-fad6-4b11-bc5a-f474bd8d3992-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/04/style/02KERING-PHOTOGRAPHER-new-girl/merlin_157294158_47449700-fad6-4b11-bc5a-f474bd8d3992-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2047, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/04/style/02KERING-PHOTOGRAPHER-new-girl/02KERING-PHOTOGRAPHER-new-girl-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/04/style/02KE