n. But he preferred the stage, and he said he had been “hugely eager” for the show to end.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Max Wright, an actor who relished his time onstage but was best known for his role as a stern father who forms an unlikely friendship with a furry extraterrestrial on the offbeat NBC sitcom “ALF,” died on June 26 at the Lillian Booth Actors Home of the Actors Fund in Englewood, N.J. He was 75.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/obituaries/28Wright/merlin_157141956_4eca593b-f5d2-4703-ac30-849f607367bc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/03/obituaries/28Wright/merlin_157141956_4eca593b-f5d2-4703-ac30-849f607367bc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/obituaries/28Wright/merlin_157141956_4eca593b-f5d2-4703-ac30-849f607367bc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/obituaries/28Wright/merlin_157141956_4eca593b-f5d2-4703-ac30-849f607367bc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1512, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/obituaries/28Wright/28Wright-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/03/obituaries/28Wright/28Wright-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/obituaries/28Wright/28Wright-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Max Wright, Who Went From Theater Roles to ‘ALF,’ Dies at 75', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Max Wright, Stage Actor  Known for a Fluffier Gig On ‘ALF,’ Is Dead at 75', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, Max (1943-2019)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'ALF (TV PROGRAM)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-02T16:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amisha Padnani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amisha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Padnani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/33435ef7-fda1-5520-8a30-f76301992a4d', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33435ef7-fda1-5520-8a30-f76301992a4d'}, {'abstract': 'One reader’s reaction: “A case of ‘Take Your Daughter to Work’ gone terribly wrong.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/02/opinion/letters/ivanka-trump-diplomat.html', 'snippet': 'One reader’s reaction: “A case of ‘Take Your Daughter to Work’ gone terribly wrong.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/01/world/01