y', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-02T18:45:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Reader Center', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a356675-3544-5e6d-b123-a85ade470f44', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a356675-3544-5e6d-b123-a85ade470f44'}, {'abstract': 'The virus has been out of the headlines, but that doesn’t mean it is gone. The World Health Organization just updated its guidelines for travelers to the Zika zone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/02/travel/traveling-zika-virus-symptoms.html', 'snippet': 'The virus has been out of the headlines, but that doesn’t mean it is gone. The World Health Organization just updated its guidelines for travelers to the Zika zone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2016, when the Zika virus first made headlines, people canceled vacations to Latin America and the Caribbean as the mosquito-borne virus spread through the region and into Texas and Florida. While the illness caused by Zika is mild, it can cause severe birth defects when pregnant women are exposed to it. But almost as quickly as it had taken over headlines, it seemed to disappear from the news. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/02/travel/02zika-travel/02zika-travel-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/02/travel/02zika-travel/02zika-travel-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/02/travel/02zika-travel/02zika-travel-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype'