 20 weeks pregnant, I and my husband learned during a routine ultrasound that our baby had not developed a major portion of her brain and  never would. The condition, anencephaly, a type of neural tube defect that also stunts the growth of the skull, is terminal. If carried to term, our baby would be very unlikely to survive for more than a few hours. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/02/opinion/02Levin/02Levin-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/02/opinion/02Levin/02Levin-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/02/opinion/02Levin/02Levin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/02/opinion/02Levin/02Levin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1421, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/02/opinion/02Levin/02Levin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/02/opinion/02Levin/02Levin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/02/opinion/02Levin/02Levin-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Shouldn’t Be Forced to Give Birth to a Baby Who Won’t Live', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANENCEPHALY', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Defects', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-03T10:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah E. Levin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Levin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0e6005b-84ef-500b-ac33-37af943d78cf', 'word_count': 874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0e6005b-84ef-500b-ac33-37af943d78cf'}, {'abstract': 'As a senator, he opposed busing and championed laws that transformed the criminal justice system. Now, as a presidential candidate, he faces renewed scrutiny over the legacy of those decisions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/03/podcasts/the-daily/joe-biden-crime-laws-race-busing.html', 'snippet': 'As a senator, he opposed busing and championed laws that transformed the criminal justice system. Now, as a presidential candidate, he faces renewed scrutiny over the legacy of those decisions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Listen and subscribe to our podcast from your mobile device: Via Apple Podcasts | Via RadioPublic | Via Stitcher', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joe Biden’s Record on Race', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headli