7/03/opinion/international-world/cuba-youth-revolution.html', 'snippet': 'The only way to change the future of Cuba is to keep raising our voices and march against the long-lived revolutionary system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HAVANA — For 12 years the government allowed a march through the streets in support of L.G.B.T.Q. rights. This year, the regime ordered its cancellation. Nevertheless, I and a group of friends joined others in May and peacefully walked seven blocks before a cordon of police officers violently shut down the march. The confrontation was just another example of a great dichotomy in Cuba, an island divided — and threatened — by age.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/opinion/03Jimenez2/merlin_153193512_9d1c4ea3-e039-4b1b-86fe-82ebfd69a2f8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/03/opinion/03Jimenez2/merlin_153193512_9d1c4ea3-e039-4b1b-86fe-82ebfd69a2f8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 422}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/opinion/03Jimenez2/merlin_153193512_9d1c4ea3-e039-4b1b-86fe-82ebfd69a2f8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/opinion/03Jimenez2/merlin_153193512_9d1c4ea3-e039-4b1b-86fe-82ebfd69a2f8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1440, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/03/opinion/03Jimenez2/03Jimenez2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumb