 two decades.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/03/books/review-i-like-to-watch-tv-revolution-emily-nussbaum.html', 'snippet': 'In “I Like to Watch,” Emily Nussbaum of The New Yorker looks back on television’s artistic high points and cultural influence over the past two decades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a quick and dirty summary of how TV has changed over the last couple of decades, just take a look at the slogans for HBO. Contrast the late-’90s snobbery of “It’s not TV. It’s HBO” with the current tagline, a warm and fuzzy declaration of feel-good humility: “It’s what connects us.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/04/books/review/03BOOKNUSSBAUM2/03BOOKNUSSBAUM2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/04/books/review/03BOOKNUSSBAUM2/03BOOKNUSSBAUM2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/04/books/review/03BOOKNUSSBAUM2/03BOOKNUSSBAUM2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/04/books/review/03BOOKNUSSBAUM2/03BOOKNUSSBAUM2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/04/books/review/03BOOKNUSSBAUM2/03BOOKNUSSBAUM2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/04/books/review/03BOOKNUSSBAUM2/03BOOKNUSSBAUM2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 