None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Big Little Lies (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-08T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ali Trachta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ali', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trachta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a44b7fce-eb2e-5626-84a3-7b474b91d551', 'word_count': 1255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a44b7fce-eb2e-5626-84a3-7b474b91d551'}, {'abstract': 'All 16 fourth-round singles matches are on the schedule, meaning you can see Roger Federer, Novak Djokovic, Rafael Nadal, Cori Gauff, Serena Williams and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/08/sports/tennis/wimbledon-what-to-watch-manic-monday.html', 'snippet': 'All 16 fourth-round singles matches are on the schedule, meaning you can see Roger Federer, Novak Djokovic, Rafael Nadal, Cori Gauff, Serena Williams and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Saturday, Federer became the first player to win 350 Grand Slam singles matches. In the final match on Centre Court today, he will face off against Berrettini, the 20th seed (third match on Centre Court, ESPN). Berrettini has enjoyed some success this year on the grass, winning the Stuttgart Open as well as reaching the semifinal at the Halle Open. However, he played a grueling five-set match against Diego Schwartzman on Saturday, which was only an hour shorter than the time that Federer has spent on court across all three of his matches. Federer’s ability to move his opponents around will be on full display as he looks to reach his sixth consecutive Wimbledon quarterfinal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': Non