7ab0794f8de'}, {'abstract': 'What’s more titillating than news spread mouth to mouth, hearsay crystallizing into legend?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/08/magazine/poem-willa-cathers-ride.html', 'snippet': 'What’s more titillating than news spread mouth to mouth, hearsay crystallizing into legend?', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s more titillating than news spread mouth to mouth, hearsay crystallizing into legend? Kim Stafford’s apocryphal account of one celebrated novelist’s beginnings unfolds as a tale within a tale, its unassuming opening drawing us in as ineluctably as the first words spun out over a campfire. As a self-proclaimed “citizen of these dark times,” Stafford, who is Oregon’s poet laureate, bears witness to the resilience of the human spirit, intertwining ordinary people’s lives with his own ardent (and unabashedly romantic) insights into the wellsprings of inspiration. I’m sure Willa Cather, passionate herald of the American frontier, would agree. Selected by Rita Dove', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/07/magazine/07mag-poem-1/07mag-poem-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 188, 'width': 285, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/07/magazine/07mag-poem-1/07mag-poem-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 188, 'width': 285, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/07/magazine/07mag-poem-1/07mag-poem-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/07/magazine/07mag-poem-1/07mag-poem-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge'