//article/3bef9e71-4415-51eb-b291-bd09a37aedd5'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Perot made a fortune in computer services, mounted bizarre paramilitary missions in Asia and was a strong third-party hopeful in the 1990s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/09/us/politics/ross-perot-death.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Perot made a fortune in computer services, mounted bizarre paramilitary missions in Asia and was a strong third-party hopeful in the 1990s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ross Perot, the wiry Texas gadfly who made a fortune in computer services, amazed the nation with audacious paramilitary missions to Vietnam and Iran, and ran for president in 1992 and 1996 with populist talk of restoring Norman Rockwell’s America, died on Tuesday at his home in Dallas. He was 89.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ross Perot, Brash Texas Billionaire Who Ran for President, Dies at 89', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ross Perot, a Blunt Billionaire Who Jolted a Race, Dies at 89', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perot, Ross', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third-Party Politics (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 1992', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reform Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-09T14:51:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert D. McFadden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None},