ine': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-07-10T03:55:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NYTNow', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melina Delkic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Delkic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c16b12f-d75e-5969-88e6-6b433c7c8529', 'word_count': 1367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c16b12f-d75e-5969-88e6-6b433c7c8529'}, {'abstract': 'Rafael Nadal, Roger Federer and Novak Djokovic find themselves on familiar ground in the men’s quarterfinals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/10/sports/tennis/wimbledon-federer-nadal-djokovic.html', 'snippet': 'Rafael Nadal, Roger Federer and Novak Djokovic find themselves on familiar ground in the men’s quarterfinals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the first match on Centre Court (8 a.m. ESPN), the world No. 1 and the defending champion, Novak Djokovic, will look to reach his fifth consecutive Grand Slam semifinal. Goffin, the 21st seed, has never reached a major semifinal. He has beaten Djokovic once in six meetings, though that victory came in their most recent match, in Monte Carlo in 2017. Goffin, normally more suited to clay and hard courts, has had a good grass-court season, reaching the final at the Halle Open, where he lost to Roger Federer. Still, Djokovic has dropped only one set on his way to the quarterfinals, and he is at ease on the surface where he has won four of his 15 major titles. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/10/sports/10tennis-watch1/merlin_157660905_61e51d94-7284-4877-bd28-e6c4f7046c83-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/1