ster-international-festival-tree-invisible-cities.html', 'snippet': '“Tree” and “Invisible Cities,” two blockbuster works, lack the impact of the festival’s more intimate experiences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, England — The play’s not quite the thing at this year’s Manchester International Festival. A showcase for homegrown and international art in this former industrial capital, it is unique in Britain for its interdisciplinary reach. Alongside the profusion of performance and visual arts, however, theater remains the festival’s main focus, and its opening weekend highlighted two ambitious yet flawed world premiere productions.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/11/arts/11manchester-festival01/11manchester-festival01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/11/arts/11manchester-festival01/11manchester-festival01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/11/arts/11manchester-festival01/11manchester-festival01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/11/arts/11manchester-festival01/11manchester-festival01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/11/arts/11manchester-festival01/11manchester-festival01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/11/a