 'snippet': 'Billboard removed Lil Nas X’s “country trap” record from a country chart. So why did Blanco Brown’s “trailertrap” song “The Git Up” make it to No. 1?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The second most-viewed version of Blanco Brown’s “The Git Up” on YouTube — after the original, audio-only clip — is a video in which he teaches the country singer Lainey Wilson the song’s accompanying dance.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/11/arts/11GITOUT/merlin_156175689_a689a6cc-9077-4dd1-8d11-7b7e8217ef32-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/11/arts/11GITOUT/merlin_156175689_a689a6cc-9077-4dd1-8d11-7b7e8217ef32-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/11/arts/11GITOUT/merlin_156175689_a689a6cc-9077-4dd1-8d11-7b7e8217ef32-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/11/arts/11GITOUT/merlin_156175689_a689a6cc-9077-4dd1-8d11-7b7e8217ef32-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/11/arts/11GITOUT/11GITOUT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/11/arts/11GITOUT/11GITOUT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/11/arts/11GITOUT/11GITOUT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Country-Rap Song Taking Over Nashville? It Isn’t ‘Old Town Road’', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How ‘The Git Up’ Bested ‘Old Town Road’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Country Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Git Up (Song)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Blanco', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Billboard (Magazine)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lil Nas X (Rapper)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Old Town Road (Song)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-11T17:54:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8718c7fb-452d-5212-982a-34b11c567e3b', 'word_count': 1067, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8718c7fb-452d-5212-982a-34b11c567e3b'}, {'abstract': 'The filmmaker and her family gathered to cook a dinner that is a nod to their grandmother’s home city of Changchun in northern China.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/11/t-magazine/entertainment/lulu-wang-the-farewell-chinese-feast.html', 'snippet': 'The filmmaker and her family gathered to cook a dinner that is a nod to their grandmother’s home city of Changchun in northern China.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Dad! You have to say he did a good job,” said the filmmaker Lulu Wang. She was addressing her father, Haiyan Wang, who was sitting next to me at dinner. It was a beautiful recent evening at the West Hollywood restaurant Auburn. A bottle of Maotai, the fiery Chinese liquor, was open, a feast of Chinese food was in front of us. Lulu has made a film about her family called “The Farewell,” which comes out this week, and I was curious whether her father liked how he was portrayed by the actor Tzi Ma. Lulu’s boyfriend, the Oscar-winning director Barry Jenkins, ever the peacemaker, chimed in: “Knowing him and knowing you, he did a good job. He’s not imitating you, he’s himself as you.” Her father nodded with a knowing smile. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/10/t-magazine/09tmag-wang-slide-EN88/09tmag-wang-slide-EN88-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/10/t-magazine/09tmag-wang-slide-EN88/09tmag-wang-slide-EN88-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/10/t-magazine/09tmag-wang-slide-EN88/09tmag-wang-slide-EN88-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/10/t-magazine/09tmag-wang-slide-EN88/09tmag-wang-slide-EN88-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/10/t-magazine/09tmag-wang-slide-EN88/09tmag-wang-slide-EN88-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'sub