d J', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vance, Cyrus R Jr', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Palm Beach (Fla)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-11T18:26:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8566be07-5a62-5c30-a9ee-1fd95a93e7e3', 'word_count': 1676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8566be07-5a62-5c30-a9ee-1fd95a93e7e3'}, {'abstract': 'At least 143 pro-government forces and 51 civilians were killed in Afghanistan during the past week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/11/magazine/afghan-war-casualty-report.html', 'snippet': 'At least 143 pro-government forces and 51 civilians were killed in Afghanistan during the past week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At least 143 pro-government forces and 52 civilians were killed in Afghanistan during another bloody week of fighting amid ongoing peace talks in Doha. The deadliest attack took place in Kunduz Province, where the Taliban attacked two military bases and several security outposts in Imam Sahib District, capturing one base and three security outposts in seven hours of fighting. At least 20 members of the security forces were killed, 15 were wounded and another 10 were taken prisoner. On Sunday, a Taliban car bomb killed 12 people in Ghazni City. Nearly 200 people were also wounded in the explosion, including more than 100 children.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/08/world/08AFGHAN-TALIBAN-02sub/merlin_157590558_a9cfa899-0616-47