istan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Improvised Explosive Devices', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Afghan National Security Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-11T18:34:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fahim Abed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fahim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/946059da-97ef-56ff-be90-d84d40b28c9b', 'word_count': 2167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/946059da-97ef-56ff-be90-d84d40b28c9b'}, {'abstract': 'Dancers swim, fish, golf and play tennis to piano pieces by Erik Satie in a light, witty opener to a strong program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/11/arts/dance/review-mark-morris-mostly-mozart.html', 'snippet': 'Dancers swim, fish, golf and play tennis to piano pieces by Erik Satie in a light, witty opener to a strong program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each of the 21 piano pieces that make up Erik Satie’s “Sports et Divertissements” has a title defining its subject: fishing, racing, tennis, golf. The program for “Sport,” Mark Morris’s new dance to the Satie score, doesn’t reproduce those titles. For this dance, such labels would be redundant.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/11/arts/11morris/merlin_157774995_071ecdea-514f-48f2-b68d-71a5dd37e54d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/11/arts/11morris/merlin_157774995_071ecdea-514f-48f2-b68d-71a5dd37e54d-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth