astname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a73fecf2-bdae-5d25-9144-2a7f8ab45bb9', 'word_count': 856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a73fecf2-bdae-5d25-9144-2a7f8ab45bb9'}, {'abstract': 'Evan Kalish starts our solving weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/11/crosswords/daily-puzzle-2019-07-12.html', 'snippet': 'Evan Kalish starts our solving weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRIDAY PUZZLE — If life was logical, the difficulty levels of crossword puzzles would get easier as the week goes on. We would start out the week with a real brain twister — sort of a multivitamin for the brain — to rev up our engines and get us primed for the week ahead. Then, after a long, busy week, we would put our feet up and solve a smooth, straightforward crossword to boost our self-confidence and let us know that, despite what might be going on in other parts of our messy lives, we succeeded in putting at least one thing in order. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/12/crosswords/12wordplay-fortyniners/merlin_65644412_496e43c1-5d33-437a-b4f7-e9698540ef95-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/12/crosswords/12wordplay-fortyniners/merlin_65644412_496e43c1-5d33-437a-b4f7-e9698540ef95-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/12/crosswords/12wordplay-fortyniners/merlin_65644412_496e43c1-5d33-437a-b4f7-e9698540ef95-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07