 region, 37 nations praised China’s “contribution to the international human rights cause.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — China fumed this week after 22 mostly Western countries rebuked its mass detention of Muslims in the restive Xinjiang region. On Friday the Chinese delivered their answer: praise from even more countries saying China has made Xinjiang safe and happy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/12/world/12china-rights/merlin_147472002_0ad4efc2-99f7-41e0-9eb1-72726d2b2370-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/12/world/12china-rights/merlin_147472002_0ad4efc2-99f7-41e0-9eb1-72726d2b2370-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/12/world/12china-rights/merlin_147472002_0ad4efc2-99f7-41e0-9eb1-72726d2b2370-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/12/world/12china-rights/merlin_147472002_0ad4efc2-99f7-41e0-9eb1-72726d2b2370-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/12/world/12china-rights/12china-rights-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/12/world/12china-rights/12china-rights-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/12/world/12china-rights/12china-rights-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Retort Over Its Mass Detentions: Praise From Russia and Saudi Arabia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beijing’s Response to Rebuke: Russian and Saudi Praise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Human Rights Council', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Xinjiang (China)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-12T19:41:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Cumming-Bruce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4f7a6ff-51ea-56f1-840f-fe2303b4120b', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4f7a6ff-51ea-56f1-840f-fe2303b4120b'}, {'abstract': 'This talking point from supporters of President Trump is wrong in several ways.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/12/us/politics/census-citizenship-obama.html', 'snippet': 'This talking point from supporters of President Trump is wrong in several ways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Trump on Thursday backed away from efforts to add a question about citizenship to the 2020 census after insisting that he would press on despite a Supreme Court ruling that the administration had not provided an adequate reason for including the question. Throughout his fight, a number of prominent conservative voices and members of his staff have amplified an inaccurate talking point that former President Barack Obama had eliminated the question. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/12/us/politics/12dc-factcheck/merlin_144005592_e23c83bf-5f46-4f8d-b8e1-c56a9076137d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/12/us/politics/12dc-factcheck/merlin_144005592_e23c83bf-5f46-4f8d-b8e1-c56a9076137d-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/12/us/politics/12dc-factcheck/merlin_144005592_e23c83bf-5f46-4f8d-b8e1-c56a9076137d-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/12/us/politics/12dc-factcheck/merlin_144005592_e23c83bf-5f46-4f8d-b8e1-c56a9076137d-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/12/us/politics/12dc-factcheck/12dc-factcheck-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/12/us/politics/12dc-factcheck/12dc-factcheck-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/12/us/politics/12dc-factcheck/12dc-factcheck-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Claims That Obama ‘Yanked’ Citizenship Question From Census Are False', 'kicker': 'Fact Check', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Census', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Census Bureau', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commerce Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Conway, Kellyanne', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Limbaugh, Rush', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-12T19:52:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Qiu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Qiu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/384e5f02-2b61-50a9-abf6-40521dbcfb89', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/384e5f02-2b61-50a9-abf6-40521dbcfb89'}, {'abstract': 'A roundup of things our editors — and a few contributors — are excited about in a given week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/12/t-magazine/t-suggests-robert-giard-ice-house-gallery.html', 'snippet': 'A roundup of things our editors — and a few contributors — are excited about in a given week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve always felt that being in a room full of queer people as a queer person creates the uncanny sensation of experiencing the past and present at the same time: L.G.B.T.Q.+ people are never not aware of the activism and its art, the homophobia and its history, the disease and its death — all those bodies missing from the room — that have spurred them to live increasingly public lives, to gather and build an ever more powerful, visible, vibrant community. I thought about this again while viewing “Particular Voices: Photographs of LGBTQ Writers, Artists and Activists, 1980s – 1990s,” a show of 53 black-and-white portrait photographs taken by Robert Giard that are on display through July 26 at Daniel Cooney’s Chelsea gallery.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/12/t-magazine/12tmag-tel-slide-U7RX/12tmag-tel-slide-U7RX-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/12/t-magazine/12tmag-tel-slide-U7RX/12tmag-tel-slide-U7RX-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/12/t-magazine/12tmag-tel-slide-U7RX/12tmag-tel-slide-U7RX-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/12/t-magazine/12tmag-tel-slide-U7RX/12tmag-tel-slide-U7RX-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/12/t-magazine/12tmag-tel-slide-U7RX/12tmag-tel-slide-U7RX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/12/t-magazine/12tmag-tel-slide-U7RX/12tmag-tel-slide-U7RX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': Non