tronaut. I want to make my India proud of me.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: Indians Put a Rover, and Their Pride, on a Rocket to the Moon', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-07-15T05:01:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/b56c49ff-4fee-5285-846e-843ec41668aa', 'word_count': 55, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b56c49ff-4fee-5285-846e-843ec41668aa'}, {'abstract': 'The hardest-hit country appeared to be Nepal, where the authorities said 67 people had died. Deaths were also reported in India and Bangladesh.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/15/world/asia/rains-nepal-india-flooding.html', 'snippet': 'The hardest-hit country appeared to be Nepal, where the authorities said 67 people had died. Deaths were also reported in India and Bangladesh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KATHMANDU, Nepal — The death toll mounted Monday from flooding and landslides caused by torrential weekend rains in India and Nepal, as rescuers carried out desperate searches for survivors and officials in nearby Bangladesh braced for the floodwaters to move downstream.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/15/world/15nepal-1/merlin_157943574_d7ba1342-b89e-4734-94bc-438b78f05481-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/15/world/15nepal-1/merlin_157943574_d7ba1342-b89e-4734-94bc-438b78f05481-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty