ec8-2d9d565b08a0', 'word_count': 1081, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efe10bad-61a3-595e-8ec8-2d9d565b08a0'}, {'abstract': 'Three artists and a pair of curators came together at The New York Times to attempt to make a list of the era’s essential artworks. Here’s their conversation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/15/t-magazine/most-important-contemporary-art.html', 'snippet': 'Three artists and a pair of curators came together at The New York Times to attempt to make a list of the era’s essential artworks. Here’s their conversation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent afternoon in June, T Magazine assembled two curators and three artists — David Breslin, the director of the collection at the Whitney Museum of American Art; the American conceptual artist Martha Rosler; Kelly Taxter, a curator of contemporary art at the Jewish Museum; the Thai conceptual artist Rirkrit Tiravanija; and the American artist Torey Thornton — at the New York Times building to discuss what they considered to be the 25 works of art made after 1970 that define the contemporary age, by anyone, anywhere. The assignment was intentionally wide in its range: What qualifies as “contemporary”? Was this an artwork that had a personal significance, or was its meaning widely understood? Was its influence broadly recognized by critics? Or museums? Or other artists? Originally, each of the participants was asked to nominate 10 artworks — the idea being that everyone would then rank each list to generate a master list that would be debated upon meeting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 25 Works of Art That Define the Contemporary Age', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asher, Michael (1943-2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bacher, Lutz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benglis, Lynda', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Birnbaum, Dara (1946- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Broodthaers, Marcel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burns, A K', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chicago, Judy', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frazier, LaToya Ruby', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldin, Nan', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gonzalez-Torres, Felix', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guston, Philip', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haacke, Hans', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hammons, David', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holzer, Jenny', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jafa, Arthur (1960- )', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelley, Mike (1954-2012)', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koons, Jeff', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kruger, Barbara', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matta-Clark, Gordon', 'rank': 21, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Noland, Cady', 'rank': 22, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Opie, Catherine', 'rank': 23, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rowland, Cameron (1988- )', 'rank': 24, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steiner, A L (1967- )', 'rank': 25, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sturtevant, Elaine (1924-2014)', 'rank': 26, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vo, Danh', 'rank': 27, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Kara', 'rank': 28, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shin, Heji (1976- )', 'rank': 29, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-15T08:57:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39c39da8-20bf-59f6-b5f5-f2d40bdb3427', 'word_count': 10807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39c39da8-20bf-59f6-b5f5-f2d40bdb3427'}, {'abstract': 'Lenses that transition in sunlight to become sunglasses help protect eyes from dust, bugs, drying breezes and, most important of all, the damaging effects of ultraviolet light.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/15/well/live/sunglasses-that-help-your-eyes-as-well-as-your-look.html', 'snippet': 'Lenses that transition in sunlight to become sunglasses help protect eyes from dust, bugs, drying breezes and, most important of all, the damaging effects of ultraviolet light.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many people my age with lens implants following cataract surgery are thrilled not to have to wear glasses all the time, but I’ve recently gone in the opposite direction. Although at 78 I can still drive and, in good light, even read the newspaper without corrective lenses, I’ve chosen to wear glasses nearly all the time.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/16/science/16BRODYSUNGLASSES/16BRODYSUNGLASSES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/16/science/16BRODYSUNGLASSES/16BRODYSUNGLASSES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/16/science/16BRODYSUNGLASSES/16BRODYSUNGLASSES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type