 show at the Queens Museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cast of the original “Star Trek” television series is the classic example of science fiction’s myopia. A mostly male, mostly white crew on an interstellar exploration vessel seems to assume that American society as it was in the 1960s could go on forever. But as an insight into the time that produced it, the vision was pretty sharp — and the same is true of the Queens Museum’s sprawling, consistently mind-bending “Mundos Alternos: Art and Science Fiction in the Americas.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/19/arts/11mundos4/merlin_157094394_8303d43b-7d84-4d9a-a0f1-150ea59c91dd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/19/arts/11mundos4/merlin_157094394_8303d43b-7d84-4d9a-a0f1-150ea59c91dd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/19/arts/11mundos4/merlin_157094394_8303d43b-7d84-4d9a-a0f1-150ea59c91dd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/19/arts/11mundos4/merlin_157094394_8303d43b-7d84-4d9a-a0f1-150ea59c91dd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/19/arts/11mundos4/11mundos4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/19/arts/11mundos4/11mundos4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnail