 singer, producer and entrepreneur has curated a show in Paris of work by the Japanese artist Mr.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Pharrell Williams has found a happy place for his inner child, and it’s a manga-style fantasy in which children have taken up arms. That’s the gist of “A Call To Action,” a new exhibition the American singer, producer and entrepreneur has curated for the Guimet Museum, a collection of Asian art here.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/23/arts/15mr-pharrell4/merlin_157772043_61a05ab1-6f2d-4d70-8924-6dd0b945dce0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/23/arts/15mr-pharrell4/merlin_157772043_61a05ab1-6f2d-4d70-8924-6dd0b945dce0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/23/arts/15mr-pharrell4/merlin_157772043_61a05ab1-6f2d-4d70-8924-6dd0b945dce0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/23/arts/15mr-pharrell4/merlin_157772043_61a05ab1-6f2d-4d70-8924-6dd0b945dce0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/23/arts/15mr-pharrell4/15mr-pharrell4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/23/arts/15mr-pharrell4/15mr-pharrell4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/23/arts/15mr-pharrell4/15mr-pharrell4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pharrell Williams Discovers His Inner Child in a Gun-Filled Manga World', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Voyage to the Depths of an Inner Child', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guimet Museum of Asian Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Pharrell', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mr (Artist) (1969- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-17T08:13:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Cappelle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cappelle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d2484ee-6442-5ae7-bc20-c1248bc3c53a', 'word_count': 897, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d2484ee-6442-5ae7-bc20-c1248bc3c53a'}, {'abstract': 'My college class asks what it means to be white in America — but interrogating that question as a black woman in the real world is much harder to do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/17/magazine/white-men-privilege.html', 'snippet': 'My college class asks what it means to be white in America — but interrogating that question as a black woman in the real world is much harder to do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the early days of the run-up to the 2016 election, I was just beginning to prepare a class on whiteness to teach at Yale University, where I had been newly hired. Over the years, I had come to realize that I often did not share historical knowledge with the persons to whom I was speaking. “What’s redlining?” someone would ask. “George Washington freed his slaves?” someone else would inquire. But as I listened to Donald Trump’s inflammatory rhetoric during the campaign that spring, the class took on a new dimension. Would my students understand the long history that informed a comment like one Trump made when he announced his presidential candidacy? “When Mexico sends its people, they’re not sending their best,” he said. “They’re sending people that have lots of problems, and they’re bringing those problems with us. They’re bringing drugs. They’re bringing crime. They’re rapists.” When I heard those words, I wanted my students to track immigration laws in the United States. Would they connect the treatment of the undocumented with the treatment of Irish, Italian and Asian people over the centuries?', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/21/magazine/21mag-privilege-promo/21mag-privilege-promo-articleLarge.png', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/21/magazine/21mag-privilege-promo/21mag-privilege-promo-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/21/magazine/21mag-privilege-promo/21mag-privilege-promo-jumbo.png', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/21/magazine/21mag-privilege-promo/21mag-privilege-promo-superJumbo.png', 'height': 810, 'width': 1440, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/21/magazine/21mag-privilege-promo/21mag-privilege-promo-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/21/magazine/21mag-privilege-promo/21mag-privilege-promo-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/21/magazine/21mag-privilege-promo/21mag-privilege-promo-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Wanted to Know What White Men Thought About Their Privilege. So I Asked.', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brief Encounters with White Men', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whites', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racial Profiling', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AFFIRMATIVE ACTION', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-17T09:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia Rankine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rankine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/146e7fc7-366f-5fe5-8f05-d6cad584b544', 'word_count': 5765, 'uri': 'nyt://article/146e7fc7-366f-5fe5-8f05-d6cad584b544'}, {'abstract': 'The V.A. was mandated to study the use of service dogs as a mental-health treatment for veterans almost a decade ago. But repeated setbacks have held up the results.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/17/magazine/service-dogs-veterans-ptsd.html', 'snippet': 'The V.A. was mandated to study the use of service dogs as a mental-health treatment for veterans almost a decade ago. But repeated setbacks have held up the results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a sunny October day in 2017, Lara Trump, the president’s daughter-in-law, held a meeting in the West Wing to promote an initiative that would pair shelter dogs needing homes with veterans wanting to act on the increasingly widespread notion that well-trained dogs can improve the lives of people suffering from post-traumatic stress disorder and other mental-health conditions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/17/magazine/17atwar-servicedog-03-copy/17atwar-servicedog-03-copy-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 483, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/17/magazine/17atwar-servicedog-03-copy/17atwar-servicedog-03-copy-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 483}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/17/magazine/17atwar-servicedog-03-copy/17atwar-servicedog-03-copy-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 825, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/17/magazine/17atwar-servicedog-03-copy/17atwar-servicedog-03-copy-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 1697, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/17/magazine/17atwar-servicedog-03-copy/17atwar-servicedog-03-copy-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 