om/2019/07/18/opinion/justice-argentina-bombing.html', 'snippet': 'Argentina is observing the grim 25th anniversary of a horrific car bombing at a Jewish community center. Its government has never arrested the culprits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUENOS AIRES — Twenty-five years after Argentina’s largest Jewish community center was bombed, murdering 85 people and wounding another 300, the cries of the dead call out to me as I walk this city’s streets, having traveled to be with Argentina’s Jewish community this week to share its grief on this terrible anniversary and to meet government officials to demand that justice finally be done.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/18/opinion/18weiss2/merlin_158071452_68c3498b-764a-483c-b2cd-a43367d5488a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 770, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/18/opinion/18weiss2/merlin_158071452_68c3498b-764a-483c-b2cd-a43367d5488a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 770}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/18/opinion/18weiss2/merlin_158071452_68c3498b-764a-483c-b2cd-a43367d5488a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 798, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/18/opinion/18weiss2/merlin_158071452_68c3498b-764a-483c-b2cd-a43367d5488a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1596, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/18/opinion/18weiss2/18weiss2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/18/opinion/18weiss2/18weiss2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/18/opinion/18weiss2/18weiss2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '85 Were Murdered in an Attack on Jews. They Deserve Justice.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Buenos Aires (Argentina)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-18T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Avi Weiss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Avi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1dd38556-965b-5170-9193-55fe5dc37c0e', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1dd38556-965b-5170-9193-55fe5dc37c0e'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge explains how she saw redemption in an inmate’s efforts to improve himself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/18/opinion/prison-drugs-freedom.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge explains how she saw redemption in an inmate’s efforts to improve himself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEST PALM BEACH, FLA. — In January 1999, Robert Clarence Potts III was sentenced to life in prison. He was 28, and had been convicted of drug and weapons charges. The federal judge sentencing him seemed to express some regret at the gravity of the penalty. But under the law at the time, Mr. Potts faced a mandatory sentence of life imprisonment without release because of the type of offenses and his tw