 to lose. When the weather’s warm and the crowd is genial, the quality of the game can feel almost superfluous. Such are the low-risk rewards of “Bottom of the 9th,” a baseball drama that finds the amiable Joe Manganiello turning his life around as a player on the fictitious Staten Island Empires.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/18/arts/18bottomof/merlin_157859421_77db5df5-52c3-462c-a80c-b621cf036b75-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/18/arts/18bottomof/merlin_157859421_77db5df5-52c3-462c-a80c-b621cf036b75-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/18/arts/18bottomof/merlin_157859421_77db5df5-52c3-462c-a80c-b621cf036b75-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/18/arts/18bottomof/merlin_157859421_77db5df5-52c3-462c-a80c-b621cf036b75-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/18/arts/18bottomof/merlin_157859421_77db5df5-52c3-462c-a80c-b621cf036b75-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/18/arts/18bottomof/merlin_157859421_77db5df5-52c3-462c-a80c-b621cf036b75-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/18/arts/18bottomof/merlin_157859421_77db5df5-52c3-462c-a80c-b621cf036b75-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Bottom of the 9th’ Review: A Stroll Around the Baseball Diamond', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bottom of the 9th', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Bottom of the 9th (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'De Felitta, Raymond', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manganiello, Joe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vergara, Sofia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-18T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Teo Bugbee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Teo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bugbee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca7ff542-59ef-5b96-8235-2b7791d169a7', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca7ff542-59ef-5b96-8235-2b7791d169a7'}, {'abstract': 'Marie Losier’s documentary steps into the ring with a Mexican professional wrestler, whose world is equal parts glamour and grunge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/18/movies/cassandro-the-exotico-review.html', 'snippet': 'Marie Losier’s documentary steps into the ring with a Mexican professional wrestler, whose world is equal parts glamour and grunge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The filmmaker Marie Losier shoots in 16 millimeter, and she clearly glories in the format. Not just the rich color saturation she squeezes from it, but the image artifacts many other camerapersons would deplore as defects. Frequently in her new documentary film, “Cassandro the Exotico!,” individual shots practically bristle with what’s called “hair in the gate” (stray fragments of celluloid that look as if they want to scour the bottom of the screen).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/19/arts/17cassandro/merlin_157859007_ec586de2-30c3-43b1-87b1-bdda0ca8517f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/19/arts/17cassandro/merlin_157859007_ec586de2-30c3-43b1-87b1-bdda0ca8517f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/19/arts/17cassandro/merlin_157859007_ec586de2-30c3-43b1-87b1-bdda0ca8517f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/19/arts/17cassandro/merlin_157859007_ec586de2-30c3-43b1-87b1-bdda0ca8517f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1280, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/19/arts/17cassandro/merlin_157859007_ec586de2-30c3-43b1-87b1-bdda0ca8517f-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/19/arts/17cassandro/merlin_157859007_ec586de2-30c3-43b1-87b1-bdda0ca8517f-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/19/arts/17cassandro/merlin_157859007_ec586de2-30c3-43b1-87b1-bdda0ca8517f-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name'