l': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/21/opinion/college-graduates-rural-america.html', 'snippet': 'You don’t have to live in a big city to succeed economically and socially.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I talk to undergraduate students about their postgraduate plans, they typically tell me about something that involves moving to a large city. They are often sure of the city even before they know what they want to do there. When I ask why they are moving to San Francisco — or Denver, or Nashville or New York — the answer inevitably reveals a common assumption: Big cities are where highly educated people must go to succeed economically and socially.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/21/opinion/21Abrams-promo/merlin_124922720_2c177b73-221f-43c6-b73d-44938cd94099-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/21/opinion/21Abrams-promo/merlin_124922720_2c177b73-221f-43c6-b73d-44938cd94099-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/21/opinion/21Abrams-promo/merlin_124922720_2c177b73-221f-43c6-b73d-44938cd94099-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/21/opinion/21Abrams-promo/merlin_124922720_2c177b73-221f-43c6-b73d-44938cd94099-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/21/opinion/21Abrams-promo/merlin_124922720_2c177b73-221f-43c6-b73d-44938cd94099-thumbStandard.j