 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the striking warnings in a recent Pentagon white paper on the growing strategic threat from Russia is that its president, Vladimir Putin, could pull a “reverse Nixon” and play his own version of the “China card” with the United States, a reference to the former president’s strategy of playing those two adversaries against each other.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/22/opinion/22chinarussiaprint/15chinarussiaWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/22/opinion/22chinarussiaprint/15chinarussiaWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/22/opinion/22chinarussiaprint/15chinarussiaWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/22/opinion/22chinarussiaprint/15chinarussiaWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1424, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/22/opinion/22chinarussiaprint/15chinarussiaWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/22/opinion/22chinarussiaprint/15chinarussiaWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/22/opinion/22chinarussiaprint/15chinarussiaWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s America’s Winning Hand if Russia Plays the China Card?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What if Russia Plays the China Card?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Strategic and International Studies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-21T23:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/31b52daf-3d5e-54e3-8f13-38666604fc9f', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31b52daf-3d5e-54e3-8f13-38666604fc9f'}, {'abstract': 'Writing a round robin letter lets senators make their views public when they can’t debate or vote on a resolution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/21/opinion/mcconnell-senate-trump-tweets.html', 'snippet': 'Writing a round robin letter lets senators make their views public when they can’t debate or vote on a resolution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was no question that the Democrats who control the House of Representatives would pass a resolution condemning President Trump’s racist tweets last week. But there was also no question that the majority leader, Mitch McConnell, would quash any attempt to even discuss a similar motion in the Senate, despite the fact that Democrats hold nearly half of the seats.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/19/opinion/19cooperWeb/merlin_158134479_74c3f5b4-17cc-4c1b-8fbb-813022bb542c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 785, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/19/opinion/19cooperWeb/merlin_158134479_74c3f5b4-17cc-4c1b-8fbb-813022bb542c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 785}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/19/opinion/19cooperWeb/merlin_158134479_74c3f5b4-17cc-4c1b-8fbb-813022bb542c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 783, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/19/opinion/19cooperWeb/merlin_158134479_74c3f5b4-17cc-4c1b-8fbb-813022bb542c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1565, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/19/opinion/19cooperWeb/19cooperWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/19/opinion/19cooperWeb/19cooperWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/19/opinion/19cooperWeb/19cooperWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width