s. This month, Benjamin Netanyahu surpassed Israel’s first prime minister, David Ben Gurion, to become the country’s longest-serving prime minister. On May 30, the Knesset dissolved itself a month after it was sworn in, making its parliamentary term the shortest in Israel’s history. This year will be the first ever with two Election Days, the one in April, the second in September.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/24/opinion/24Rosner1/merlin_158104023_71714813-0fb0-4d94-b139-0f39032e7ba8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/24/opinion/24Rosner1/merlin_158104023_71714813-0fb0-4d94-b139-0f39032e7ba8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/24/opinion/24Rosner1/merlin_158104023_71714813-0fb0-4d94-b139-0f39032e7ba8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/24/opinion/24Rosner1/merlin_158104023_71714813-0fb0-4d94-b139-0f39032e7ba8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1287, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/24/opinion/24Rosner1/24Rosner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/24/opinion/24Rosner1/24Rosner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/24/opinion/24Rosner1/24Rosner1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Last Thing Israel Needs Is Yet Another Election', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blue and White (Israeli Political Party)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Likud Party (Israel)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gantz, Benny', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-24T05:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shmuel Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shmuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fe1a501-f6d9-56f2-b683-f74008c832aa', 'word_count': 1007, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fe1a501-f6d9-56f2-b683-f74008c832aa'}, {'abstract': 'A new documentary on Netflix looks at the Cambridge Analytica scandal. And Anne Hathaway stars opposite Matthew McConaughey in “Serenity.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/24/arts/television/whats-on-tv-wednesday-the-great-hack-and-serenity.html', 'snippet': 'A new documentary on Netflix looks at the Cambridge Analytica scandal. And Anne Hathaway stars opposite Matthew McConaughey in “Serenity.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE GREAT HACK (2019) Stream on Netflix. In her 2013 documentary, “The Square,” the director Jehane Noujaim captured Egypt from the winter of 2011 to the summer of 2013, during a time of political unrest and revolution lubricated by social media. The results of Noujaim’s work, A.O. Scott wrote in his review for The New York Times, were “stunning.” This new documentary, made by Noujaim and the filmmaker Karim Amer, is more directly concerned with social networks: It turns its attention to the commodification of personal data, with a focus on the Cambridge Analytica scandal and the way American Facebook users’ data was harvested in the lead-up to the 2016 election. The principal figure through which that story gets dissected is Brittany Kaiser, a former Cambridge Analytica executive who became an outspoken defector. Also interviewed are the whistle-blower Christopher Wylie and the journalist Carole Cadwalladr, who was an author of a collaborative report between The Times and The Observer that exposed how Cambridge Analytica harvested the information of tens of millions of Facebook users. In that article, Wylie described the company as an “arsenal of weapons” in a culture war. This documentary picks apart those weapons, and their effects.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/24/arts/24tvcol-thegreathack/24tvcol-thegreathack-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/24/arts/24tvcol-thegreathack/24tvcol-thegreathack-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/24/arts/24tvcol-thegreathack/24tvcol-thegreathack-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i