tephen Castle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/974758c3-67e7-5024-ac80-62c97286a00e', 'word_count': 1227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/974758c3-67e7-5024-ac80-62c97286a00e'}, {'abstract': 'This month brings the debut of two very different shows by Bashir Salahuddin and Diallo Riddle: “South Side” on Comedy Central and “Sherman’s Showcase” on IFC.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/24/arts/television/south-side-shermans-showcase.html', 'snippet': 'This month brings the debut of two very different shows by Bashir Salahuddin and Diallo Riddle: “South Side” on Comedy Central and “Sherman’s Showcase” on IFC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — One afternoon last month, driving down 87th Street in the Auburn Gresham neighborhood where he was raised on Chicago’s South Side, the comedic writer and actor Bashir Salahuddin glanced out the window of his chauffeured S.U.V., noticed an underpass with the neighborhood’s name spelled out in graffiti on it, and smiled. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/25/arts/22southside-feature1/22southside-feature1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/25/arts/22southside-feature1/22southside-feature1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/25/arts/22southside-feature1/22southside-feature1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/25/arts/22southside-feature1/22southside-feature1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1638, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/25/arts/22southside-feature1/22southside-feature1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/25/arts/22southside-feature1/22southside-feature1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/25/arts/22southside-feature1/22southside-feature1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Two TV Writers Scored Two Series After Years of Struggle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Writing Team Strikes Twice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'South Side (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Sherman's Showcase (TV Program)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salahuddin, Bashir', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Riddle, Diallo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-24T08:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Hyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3002423e-0f1d-5215-97fc-c9c7dd989cb3', 'word_count': 1428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3002423e-0f1d-5215-97fc-c9c7dd989cb3'}, {'abstract': 'A sizzling platter of bright red chicken drenched in a thick, fragrant sauce tempered by mozzarella.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/24/magazine/korean-fire-chicken-cheese-buldak-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'A sizzling platter of bright red chicken drenched in a thick, fragrant sauce tempered by mozzarella.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I first laid eyes on cheese buldak, a mozzarella-cloaked Korean dish that translates as “fire chicken,” in a 24-hour restaurant off Wilshire Boulevard in Los Angeles. It was very late at night, and a couple in a window table were pulling long strings of melting cheese off a sizzling platter that beneath its glistening white blanket revealed a steaming pile of bright red chicken drenched in a thick, fragrant sauce. The couple appeared to be in a kind of happy daze, eating silently, mopping their brows, checking the social media feeds on their phones and then returning to the cheese, the chicken, an occasional bite of rice. My ox-bone soup, light and restorative, seemed flat by comparison. I became bored by it, and clomped off into the darkness. I’d made a mistake in ordering and was filled with regret.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/28/dining/28mag-eat/28mag-eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 443, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/28/dining/28mag-eat/28mag-eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 443}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/28/dining/28mag-eat/28mag-eat-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 756, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/28/dining/28mag-eat/28mag-eat-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1513, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Melt Away the Pain of This Korean Fire Chicken With Cheese', 'kicker': 'Eat ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Korean-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheese', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Korean Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-24T09:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a64c94d0-342c-573a-aa44-9ea08c16e43e', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a64c94d0-342c-573a-aa44-9ea08c16e43e'}, {'abstract': '“If you lived my life, you would drink, too.” I knew I was an alcoholic, but under no terms did I want to do anything about it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/24/magazine/alcohol-sobriety-military.html', 'snippet': '“If you lived my life, you would drink, too.” I knew I was an alcoholic, but under no terms did I want to do anything about it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sept. 29, 2016, I was at a private book signing in Williamson County, Tenn., for Alberto Gonzales, the former United States attorney general. As the chairwoman for the Montgomery County Young Republicans, I spent a lot of time sharing drinks with Tennessee’s political class. At the end of the evening, I decided to drive home, even though I knew I had drunk too much. I had taken these back roads so many times, I told myself; I could make it home. Twenty minutes into my hourlong trek, I passed out. When I regained consciousness, I was upside down in a ditch. A stranger stopped to pull me out of my car. The police arrived and arrested me immediately. The next morning, reality set in. I had done so much damage in my life that my son, Taj, who was 16 at the time, refused to talk to me. That was the last night I drank.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/23/magazine/23atwar-sobriety-1/23atwar-sobriety-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/23/magazine/23atwar-sobriety-1/23atwar-sobriety-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/23/magazine/23atwar-sobriety-1/23atwar-sobriety-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/23/magazine/23atwar-sobriety-1/23atwar-sobriety-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/23/magazine/23atwar-sobriety-1/23atwar-sobriety-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/23/magazine/23atwar-sobriety-1/23atwar-sobriety-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75,