uri': 'nyt://article/5b5918fa-da45-577e-a66a-1ab8736d033f'}, {'abstract': 'The master filmmaker’s “Summer Interlude,” “Summer With Monika” and “Smiles of a Summer Night” evoke the transitory happiness of the brief, intense Nordic summer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/24/arts/ingmar-bergman-summer-movies.html', 'snippet': 'The master filmmaker’s “Summer Interlude,” “Summer With Monika” and “Smiles of a Summer Night” evoke the transitory happiness of the brief, intense Nordic summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fleeting Nordic summer, a respite from the darkness of interminable winter, is “the loveliest time of the year,” the Swedish author Selma Lagerlof wrote, with some understatement, in “The Story of Gosta Berling”: “Everything was beautiful. The road, gray and dusty as it was, had its border of flowers.” Even “the smallest child went on the road with a bunch of lilacs in her hand, and every peasant woman had a little bouquet stuck in her neckerchief.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/28/arts/28HOBERMAN-STREAMING-1/merlin_158030745_aea9a71c-1872-433d-a74c-2cf6db84679d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/28/arts/28HOBERMAN-STREAMING-1/merlin_158030745_aea9a71c-1872-433d-a74c-2cf6db84679d-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 411}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/28/arts/28HOBERMAN-STREAMING-1/merlin_158030745_aea9a71c-1872-433d-a74c-2cf6db84679d-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/28/arts/28HOBERMAN-STREAMING-1/merlin_158030745_aea9a7