], 'pub_date': '2019-07-25T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Live', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toby Bilanow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilanow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4945f70-c522-5d35-9e94-cbc7d7967958', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4945f70-c522-5d35-9e94-cbc7d7967958'}, {'abstract': 'Should the dogs be involved in a dispute about disgusting mouth noises?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/25/magazine/judge-john-hodgman-on-the-sound-of-flossing.html', 'snippet': 'Should the dogs be involved in a dispute about disgusting mouth noises?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kyle writes: My wife suffers from misophonia, and the sound of dental flossing is a trigger. I floss behind a closed door two rooms away, but she sometimes walks into the adjacent room and complains to our dogs about the noise. I don’t think she should be allowed to bad-mouth me when I’m going out of my way to be nice.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/magazine/Mag-Hodgman-1/Mag-Hodgman-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/12/magazine/Mag-Hodgman-1/Mag-Hodgman-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/magazine/Mag-Hodgman-1/Mag-Hodgman-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/magaz