'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenigsberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/add63227-27cc-5134-97a4-6dfe08e9f202', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/add63227-27cc-5134-97a4-6dfe08e9f202'}, {'abstract': 'It’s hard to stand still when you have troublesome co-workers, a mentally ill sister and the need for exercise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/25/movies/the-ground-beneath-my-feet-review.html', 'snippet': 'It’s hard to stand still when you have troublesome co-workers, a mentally ill sister and the need for exercise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are some things worse than hacking one’s way through a gig economy, particularly if you’re a woman. Take the case of Lola Wegenstein, who’s trying to find stability in multinational corporate hell. Beautifully played by Valerie Pachner in this searing film written and directed by Marie Kreutzer, Lola is attractive, intelligent, and health conscious — the opening scene shows her on a morning run. She’s also a walking ball of anxiety in her professional role at a high-powered consulting firm that trims the fat from troubled companies.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/26/arts/25thegroundbeneath/merlin_158307819_c4f85261-7029-4b71-bf41-1b5f0bcfb6ad-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/26/arts/25thegroundbeneath/merlin_158307819_c4f85261-7029-4b71-bf41-1b5f0bcfb6ad-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/26/arts/25thegroundbeneath/merlin_158307819_c4f85261-7029-4b71-bf41-1b5f0bcfb6ad-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 539, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/26/arts/25thegroundbeneath/merlin_158307819_c4f85261-7029-4b71-bf41-1b5f0bcfb6ad-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1078, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/26/arts/25thegroundbeneath/25thegroundbeneath-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/26/arts/25thegroundbeneath/25thegroundbeneath-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/26/arts/25thegroundbeneath/25thegroundbeneath-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Ground Beneath My Feet’ Review: A Woman on the Run', 'kicker': 'CRITIC’s PICK', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Perpetual Motion Is Her Best Defense', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Ground Beneath My Feet (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kreutzer, Marie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pachner, Valerie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hierzegger, Pia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-25T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6173d19-a9a2-5ddc-a776-a23810c23ce0', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6173d19-a9a2-5ddc-a776-a23810c23ce0'}, {'abstract': 'This film, set almost entirely in Afghanistan, features striking landscapes that are rarely seen onscreen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/25/movies/jirga-review.html', 'snippet': 'This film, set almost entirely in Afghanistan, features striking landscapes that are rarely seen onscreen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The real Kabul and Kandahar are almost never seen in contemporary movies, particularly those produced in the West. So the sense of going somewhere you’ve never been is palpable from almost the very beginning of “Jirga,” a fictional film shot almost entirely in and around these cities in Afghanistan.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/26/arts/25jirga1/merlin_158307906_640dc953-a3dc-4e93-a1c9-57d23cc5131d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/26/arts/25jirga1/merlin_158307906_640dc953-a3dc-4e93-a1c9-57d23cc5131d-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/26/arts/25jirga1/merlin_158307906_640dc953-a3dc-4e93-a1c9-57d23cc5131d-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/26/arts/25jirga1/merlin_158307906_640dc953-a3dc-4e93-a1c9-57d23cc5131d-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1050, 'width': 1868, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0