ne}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dca7b97-c677-5c10-b8e2-0ba6d103c743', 'word_count': 667, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dca7b97-c677-5c10-b8e2-0ba6d103c743'}, {'abstract': 'A downside of social living among monkeys and chimpanzees, a new study suggests, is being at greater risk of deadly disease.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/25/science/monkeys-anthrax-flies.html', 'snippet': 'A downside of social living among monkeys and chimpanzees, a new study suggests, is being at greater risk of deadly disease.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the jungles of Ivory Coast, monkeys and chimps forage for food, sleep in trees and travel in groups. Not far behind follow primatologists, like Jan Gogarten, a postdoctoral researcher at the Robert Koch Institute in Germany.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/30/science/25TB-MONKEYFLIES1b/25TB-MONKEYFLIES1b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/30/science/25TB-MONKEYFLIES1b/25TB-MONKEYFLIES1b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/30/science/25TB-MONKEYFLIES1b/25TB-MONKEYFLIES1b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/30/science/25TB-MONKEYFLIES1b/25TB-MONKEYFLIES1b-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/30/science/25TB-MONKEYFLIES1b/25TB-MONKEYFLIES1b-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'wi