 'pub_date': '2019-07-25T21:07:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6c01d08-ce64-54af-9808-af8155f053b7', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6c01d08-ce64-54af-9808-af8155f053b7'}, {'abstract': 'The iPhone maker is adding patents and 2,200 Intel employees as it tries to reduce dependency on another chip maker, Qualcomm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/25/technology/apple-pays-1-billion-for-part-of-intels-modem-business.html', 'snippet': 'The iPhone maker is adding patents and 2,200 Intel employees as it tries to reduce dependency on another chip maker, Qualcomm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Apple said on Thursday that it would buy most of Intel’s smartphone-modem business for $1 billion, aiding its push to gain more control over faster wireless technology in iPhones.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple Pays $1 Billion for Part of Intel’s Modem Business', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Apple to Pay $1 Billion For Key Piece of Intel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intel Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '5G (Wireless Communications)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-25T21:13:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Nicas and Don Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nicas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Don', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bfd1505-d292-5e8b-9ef6-e8fce2f49fc7', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bfd1505-d292-5e8b-9ef6-e8fce2f49fc7'}, {'abstract': 'There is a more glaring reason to impeach Trump: racism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/25/opinion/mueller-trump-impeach-racism.html', 'snippet': 'There is a more glaring reason to impeach Trump: racism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One day, browsing Tinder, imagine that you come upon the profile of an obese, orange-haired real estate magnate and proud, raging racist. The first line of his bio: “Mexicans are rapists.” Formative business experience: Not renting to blacks. One of his profile pictures is a hand drawing of the continent of Africa across which he has scrawled the word “shithole.” Muslims: Don’t let them in. Jews, he tolerates, because sometimes you need a lawyer or an accountant, but he will also give a fair hearing to the very fine people who hate Jews. For this guy, anyone of color should be viewed always and entirely through the lens of that color, laboring permanently under a cloud of suspicion: Check their birth certificate. Hold them in cages. Send them back.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/25/opinion/25manjooWeb/25manjooWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width':