6a9b-5246-a43d-191095460a90'}, {'abstract': 'Exposure to art — even uncomfortable art — is healthy, stimulating, and worthy of students’ debate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/26/arts/design/george-washington-san-francisco-murals.html', 'snippet': 'Exposure to art — even uncomfortable art — is healthy, stimulating, and worthy of students’ debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After half a century of intermittent debate and protest, the San Francisco Board of Education voted unanimously in June to whitewash the 13 murals depicting the life of George Washington that line the halls of a high school named for the first president. The murals’ offense is that they depict some ugly truths about the history of the United States, namely two of its original sins: slavery and the Native American genocide. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/27/multimedia/26SFMURAL-promo/27xp-Murals-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/06/27/multimedia/26SFMURAL-promo/27xp-Murals-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/27/multimedia/26SFMURAL-promo/27xp-Murals-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/27/multimedia/26SFMURAL-promo/27xp-Murals-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/06/27/multimedia/26SFMURAL-promo/26SFMURAL-promo-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'widt