525511_fefa8e54-3d8f-4b92-b852-c887ff69c52f-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clashes and Tear Gas as Hong Kong Police Confront Protesters in Yuen Long', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clashes and Tear Gas as Hong Kong Police Confront Protesters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yuen Long (Hong Kong)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tear Gas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hong Kong Protests (2019)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-27T04:01:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Ramzy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramzy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42d8e8e0-1428-5550-87dd-1d5b904020bf', 'word_count': 1160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42d8e8e0-1428-5550-87dd-1d5b904020bf'}, {'abstract': 'Pippa Bianco’s debut feature about sexual assault and memory comes to HBO, and Viola Davis’s heist drama is available to stream.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/27/arts/television/whats-on-tv-saturday-share-and-widows.html', 'snippet': 'Pippa Bianco’s debut feature about sexual assault and memory comes to HBO, and Viola Davis’s heist drama is available to stream.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHARE 10 p.m. on HBO. This feature debut from the writer-director Pippa Bianco is an unflinching look at sexual assault in the digital age. The film opens with a 16-year-old, Mandy (Rhianne Barreto), waking up on her front lawn after a night of partying, not sure how she got there. In the morning, she receives a barrage of text massages from friends alerting her to a grainy video that’s been circulating. It shows Mandy lying on the floor unconscious, while her crush (Nicholas Galitzine) removes her clothes. But it’s what the video doesn’t show that propels the film, as Mandy works to uncover the truth, growing more isolated in the process. “Bianco uses a depressingly familiar story of high-school partying gone wrong to explore sometimes uncomfortable questions about gender, agency and collective guilt,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. The film joins “The Tale” and the gritty teen drama “Euphoria” in HBO’s catalog of female-led stories about sexual assault, anxiety and the unreliability of memory.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/27/arts/27tvcol-share/27tvcol-share-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/27/arts/27tvcol-share/27tvcol-share-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/27/arts/27tvcol-share/27tvcol-share-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/27/arts/27tvcol-share/27tvcol-share-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJum