jor': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-29T23:15:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mujib Mashal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mujib', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mashal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21a622ae-c478-5cb6-bd01-4febce217e93', 'word_count': 1286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21a622ae-c478-5cb6-bd01-4febce217e93'}, {'abstract': 'Kahkow in Williamsburg is owned by Rizek Cacao from the Dominican Republic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/29/dining/kahkow-brooklyn-dominican-republic-chocolate.html', 'snippet': 'Kahkow in Williamsburg is owned by Rizek Cacao from the Dominican Republic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rizek Cacao, a chocolate grower, processor and exporter, was founded in the Dominican Republic in 1905 and is now being run by the fifth generation of the Rizek family. The company owns 25 farms on the island and contract with another 2,500 small farmers to whom they provide technical support through a nonprofit organization. Rizek processes cacao and sells wholesale to other chocolate companies. In 2007, it began making bars for the consumer market, sold only in the Dominican Republic, and now it has opened its first boutique abroad. At the shop and cafe in Brooklyn chocolate for cooks, finished bars, other ingredients, and some baked goods are sold, though Nadia Rizek, a family member, said the main purpose of the store was education. Soon the cafe expects to start roasting cacao on the premises.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/dining/31Burner-coco/merlin_158389425_9d4eaca5-76a3-40ab-bb3c-cf9f6861093e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/31/dining/31Burner-coco/merlin_158389425_9d4eaca5-76a3-40ab-bb3c-cf9f6861093e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/dining/31Burner-coco/merlin_158389425_9d4eaca5-76a3-40ab-bb3c-cf9f6861093e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/dining/31Burner-coco/merlin_158389425_9d4eaca5-76a3-40ab-bb3c-cf9f6861093e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/dining/31Burner-coco/31Burner-coco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/31/dining/31Burner-coco/31Burner-coco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/dining/31Burner-coco/31Burner-coco-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brooklyn Gets a Dominican Chocolate Shop', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sample: Dominican Chocolate Shop Opens in Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kahkow (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chocolate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rizek Cacao SAS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-29T23:15:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e40317e-fe4c-5b6b-a4f9-edabe8da5fe6', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e40317e-fe4c-5b6b-a4f9-edabe8da5fe6'}, {'abstract': 'Alice Feiring’s new book takes a deep dive into the additive-free world of winemaking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/29/dining/drinks/natural-wine-for-the-people-book-alice-feiring.html', 'snippet': 'Alice Feiring’s new book takes a deep dive into the additive-free world of winemaking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In her slender new book, the wine writer Alice Feiring deconstructs natural wine, the trend that’s sweeping the wine world. Ms. Feiring, whose middle name should be “terroir,” starts by describing what natural wine is not: It lacks the fruit, power and oak of some high-end wines. Ms. Feiring takes the same approach to wine as she does to food, avoiding anything highly processed and additive-laden, and explains all the additives used in conventional wine production that natural winemakers don’t use. But she also gets into weedy details; amateurs might prefer to ignore sections on stuff like reverse-osmosis and infusion, and concentrate instead on how wine gets its color, the use or presence of sulfur in wine, how to find natural wines and why you should care. And if you’re planning a trip to France or a few other countries and want to visit natural wineries, she includes some guidance.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/dining/29burner4/29burner4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 321, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/31/dining/29burner4/29burner4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 321}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/dining/29burner4/29burner4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 548, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/dining/29burner4/29burner4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1096, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/dining/29burner4/29burner4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/31/dining/29burner4/29burner4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/dining/29burner4/29burner4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Natural Wines, Explained', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Appreciate: A Deep Dive Into Natural Wines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feiring, Alice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ten Speed Press', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Natural Wine for the People: What It Is, Where to Find It, How to Love It (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-29T23:18:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Wine, Beer & Cocktails', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34f5a545-397e-53dc-b81e-5888e68ac62e', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34f5a545-397e-53dc-b81e-5888e68ac62e'}, {'abstract': 'Chiles and crushed maguey worms create an incomparable salt, sal de gusano, for elotes, margaritas and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/29/dining/sal-de-gusano-mexican-salt.html', 'snippet': 'Chiles and crushed maguey worms create an incomparable salt, sal de gusano, for elotes, margaritas and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Flavored salts, in my view, simply clutter the kitchen counter. If you have good sea salt and high-quality herbs or spices on hand, there’s no trick to creating your own. But there are exceptions, like this one, new to our pantries, from Oaxaca, Mexico, which combines salt with pequín and arból chiles and dried, crushed maguey worms. Yes, of course, dust the tangy, earthily assertive and fragrant rust-colored spice on the edge of your margarita glass, but also consider it for seasoning corn on the cob, ceviche or grilled shrimp. Christopher Kimball is selling it on his Milk Street website.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/di