ant called the Fulton.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/30/dining/the-fulton-review-pete-wells-jean-georges.html', 'snippet': 'Out on Pier 17 in the seaport district, Jean-Georges Vongerichten has opened a seafood restaurant called the Fulton.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sooner or later, those of us who follow the career of Jean-Georges Vongerichten reach a point where our memories can’t keep up. The tuna tartares start to run together; we can’t recall whether it’s served in lettuce cups with threads of shiso at Perry St. or at JoJo. At some point it’s hard to recall what makes the chicken breast inside a resoundingly crunchy Parmesan crust at Nougatine different from the Parmesan-crusted chicken at the Mark.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/30/dining/30REST-SLIDESHOW-slide-L4HA/30REST-SLIDESHOW-slide-L4HA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/30/dining/30REST-SLIDESHOW-slide-L4HA/30REST-SLIDESHOW-slide-L4HA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/30/dining/30REST-SLIDESHOW-slide-L4HA/30REST-SLIDESHOW-slide-L4HA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/30/dining/30REST-SLIDESHOW-slide-L4HA/30REST-SLIDESHOW-slide-L4HA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/30/dining/30REST-SLIDESHOW-slide-L4HA/30REST-SLIDESHOW-slide-L4HA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/30/dining/30REST-SLIDESHOW-slide-L4HA/30REST-SLIDESHOW-slide-L4HA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/30/dining/30REST-SLIDESHOW-slide-L4HA/30REST-SLIDESHOW-slide-L4HA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For the Freshest Fish, Head to the East River', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Freshest Catch Along the East River', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vongerichten, Jean-Georges', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'The Fulton (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Street Seaport (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paris Cafe (Queens, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-30T16:40:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/37441ca0-3ad5-5993-aace-a1d3cd17adee', 'word_count': 1247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37441ca0-3ad5-5993-aace-a1d3cd17adee'}, {'abstract': 'Tasting menus from stalwarts of high-end dining, a charming downtown French spot and more restaurant news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/30/dining/nyc-restaurant-news.html', 'snippet': 'Tasting menus from stalwarts of high-end dining, a charming downtown French spot and more restaurant news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A number of the restaurants at Hudson Yards have views of the river, but none offer the sweep of this new 24th-floor terraced dining room. It’s part of the flagship restaurant in the new Equinox Hotel. Despite its name, which seems to nod to psychedelic, acid-dropping counterculture, it’s part of a clean-living fitness organization and has a fresh, local approach to food. The chef, Kyle Knall, a native of Birmingham, Ala., worked at Gramercy Tavern and the now-closed Maysville. With Sean Joseph, a partner in Maysville, he also opened Kenton’s in New Orleans, which closed last year. Now Mr. Knall is with Starr Restaurants, which runs food and drink service for the Equinox. Hay-roasted oysters, beef tartare, black bass with a salsa verde, roasted trout with “green things from the garden,” and grilled and braised lamb with roasted eggplant, cumin and sumac, are some of the dishes to be savored at tables in the sleek dining room or on the expansive terrace. (Opens Thursday) ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/dining/30off/merlin_158484321_70cc2842-9046-423b-bd5c-4003669f3dcc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/31/dining/30off/merlin_158484321_70cc2842-9046-423b-bd5c-4003669f3dcc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/dining/30off/merlin_158484321_70cc2842-9046-423b-bd5c-4003669f3dcc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None,