type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ad1142d-1f44-52ea-9b0a-e9296f173b9e', 'word_count': 2146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ad1142d-1f44-52ea-9b0a-e9296f173b9e'}, {'abstract': 'The first debate exchange captured the battle within the Democratic Party over how the presidential nominee should change the country’s health care system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/30/us/politics/sanders-delaney-health-care.html', 'snippet': 'The first debate exchange captured the battle within the Democratic Party over how the presidential nominee should change the country’s health care system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first exchange of the Democratic presidential debate on Tuesday offered a quick and exacting look at the vast ideological divide between the progressive wing of the Democratic Party and the more moderate candidates on the central topic of health care.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watch Bernie Sanders and John Delaney Battle Over Medicare for All', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Delaney, John R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-31T00:44:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8dd4a218-d15a-5974-b56f-1b75adb0f344', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8dd4a218-d15a-5974-b56f-1b75adb0f344'}, {'abstract': 'Moderate underdogs kicked off the Detroit debates by targeting the top candidates with charges of “wish-list economics” and “impossible promises” on health care.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/30/us/politics/democratic-presidential-debate-recap.html', 'snippet': 'Moderate underdogs kicked off the Detroit debates by targeting the top candidates with charges of “wish-list economics” and “impossible promises” on health care.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — The leading liberals in the Democratic presidential primary, Senators Bernie Sanders and Elizabeth Warren, strenuously fought back on Tuesday against accusations of making fanciful promises and imperiling the party’s prospects against President Trump, as a group of moderate underdogs sought to slow their momentum in the second round of debates.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sanders and Warren Battle Accusations of ‘Fairy Tale’ Promises as Intraparty Rift Flares', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leading Liberals  Fend Off Attacks  On Big Promises ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-31T01:13:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics