 York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Child Victims Act (2019)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Kat', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joint Commission on Public Ethics (NYS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Outdoor Advertising', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-31T09:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Wang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccf2f941-c304-507c-849b-04d67376e720', 'word_count': 1222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccf2f941-c304-507c-849b-04d67376e720'}, {'abstract': 'Posters from 1918 reveal ignorance of the toll that the war took on those who fought it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/31/magazine/world-war-i-veterans-treatment.html', 'snippet': 'Posters from 1918 reveal ignorance of the toll that the war took on those who fought it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The shelling stopped on Nov. 11, 1918, sending millions of American soldiers back to the United States to pick up where they had left off before joining or being drafted into the war effort. For one officer, the return meant facing a perfunctory public welcome and superficial support. “The quick abandonment of interest in our overseas men by Americans in general,” he observed three years after the Armistice, “is an indictment against us as a nation, not soon to be forgotten by the men in uniform from the other side.” The soldier, a former Army officer later identified as Herbert B. Hayden, anonymously published his observations in an essay for The Atlantic Monthly. The severe effects of combat-related injuries, like the ones Hayden described in his essay, drew more public attention during the 1920s, when the figure of the shellshocked veteran became part of larger debates over the government’s responsibility to care for its military forces.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/magazine/31atwar-WWIPOSTERS3-image-02/31atwar-WWIPOSTERS3-image-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 472, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/31/magazine/31atwar-WWIPOSTERS3-image-02/31atwar-WWIPOSTERS3-image-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 472}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/magazine/31atwar-WWIPOSTERS3-image-02/31atwar-WWIPOSTERS3-image-02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 806, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/magazine/31atwar-WWIPOSTERS3-image-02/31atwar-WWIPOSTERS3-image-02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1574, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/magazine/31atwar-WWIPOSTERS3-image-02/31atwar-WWIPOSTERS3-image-02-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': 