organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87d78b93-cc6b-56c6-9a96-ecf9d1c7fa30', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87d78b93-cc6b-56c6-9a96-ecf9d1c7fa30'}, {'abstract': 'It’s not spicy hot but has a magnificent warmth. Quick-pickled fresh ripe bananas add a creamy bland sweetness with a spike of vinegar and habanero.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/31/magazine/jerk-chicken-recipe-summer-camp.html', 'snippet': 'It’s not spicy hot but has a magnificent warmth. Quick-pickled fresh ripe bananas add a creamy bland sweetness with a spike of vinegar and habanero.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The one and only summer I went to sleepaway camp, I bunked with these ferocious girls from Morris County, in New Jersey, who wore tubes of grape-scented Lip Smacker lip gloss on lanyards that hung from their necks and who hogged the bank of bathroom mirrors blow-drying their hair every afternoon before dinner. The one girl I did love, a freckled, husky tomboy, packed her rucksack and ran away right after our counselor’s flashlight bed check one night, and I wept silent, racking sobs in my lower bunk until dawn, terrified for her out in the wilderness. Or worse, wandering onto 95 South with all those long-haul 18-wheelers pounding the uncongested Interstate in the dark hours.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/04/magazine/04mag-eat/04mag-eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/04/magazine/04mag-eat/04mag-eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/04/magazine/04mag-eat/04mag-eat-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/04/magazine/04mag-eat/04mag-eat-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/04/magazine/04mag-eat/04mag-eat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/08/04/magazine/04mag-eat/04mag-eat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/04/magazine/04mag-eat/04mag-eat-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jerk Chicken So Good I’ve Been Making It Every Summer for 25 Years', 'kicker': 'Eat ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jerk Chicken So Good I’ve Been Making It Every Summer for 25 Years', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Camps and Camping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chickens', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-31T13:08:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gabrielle Hamilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabrielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hamilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91ad5b9a-b02d-5d01-a787-ab9a4ebfc47b', 'word_count': 876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91ad5b9a-b02d-5d01-a787-ab9a4ebfc47b'}, {'abstract': 'Competition among these male spiders is fierce. So suitors take advantage of clues left by their reproductive rivals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/31/science/black-widow-spider-males.html', 'snippet': 'Competition among these male spiders is fierce. So suitors take advantage of clues left by their reproductive rivals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a myth that black widow female spiders always kill and consume their mates. But courtship remains perilous for males, cannibalism or no. The terrain, navigated in the dark, is challenging. The female’s web releases come-hither pheromones, but only about 12 percent of prospective males manage to reach it. And once there, they can expect to face male rivals competing to pass their genes on to the next generation.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/06/science/30TB-SPIDERS1/30TB-SPIDERS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/08/06/science/30TB-SPIDERS1/30TB-SPIDERS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/06/science/30TB-SPIDERS1/30TB-SPIDERS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/06/science/30TB-SPIDERS1/30TB-SPIDERS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/08/06/science/30TB-SPIDERS1/30TB-SPIDERS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_na