.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a fictionalized version of a notorious crime story, directed by a top-brand filmmaker, and the starry ensemble includes Al Pacino. No, it’s not Quentin Tarantino’s “Once Upon a Time … in Hollywood.” Rather, it’s Martin Scorsese’s “The Irishman,” a Netflix release that covers the 1975 disappearance of Jimmy Hoffa and features two of the director’s most celebrated collaborators, Robert De Niro and Joe Pesci, along with Pacino, who has never worked with Scorsese before.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/arts/31irishman-trailer1/31irishman-trailer1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 313, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/31/arts/31irishman-trailer1/31irishman-trailer1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 313}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/arts/31irishman-trailer1/31irishman-trailer1-jumbo.png', 'height': 534, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/arts/31irishman-trailer1/31irishman-trailer1-superJumbo.png', 'height': 658, 'width': 1262, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/arts/31irishman-trailer1/31irishman-trailer1-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/31/arts/31irishman-trailer1/31irishman-trailer1-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/ar