cle/df72ac94-de13-5db6-955a-432ff2d0845d'}, {'abstract': 'Candidates are promising a kind of change that history suggests they cannot deliver.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/31/opinion/2020-democrats-change-structural.html', 'snippet': 'Candidates are promising a kind of change that history suggests they cannot deliver.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the Democratic race for the 2020 presidential nomination heats up, a newly fashionable term has entered the political lexicon: “structural.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/opinion/31gross/31gross-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/31/opinion/31gross/31gross-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/opinion/31gross/31gross-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/opinion/31gross/31gross-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1379, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/opinion/31gross/31gross-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/07/31/opinion/31gross/31gross-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/opinion/31gross/31gross-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Do the Democrats Keep Saying ‘Structural’?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sociology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-07-31T15:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Gross', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gross', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d59d5dd8-d8a9-5005-bd84-7ef52b3ce1ca', 'word_count': 1067, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d59d5dd8-d8a9-5005-bd84-7ef52b3ce1ca'}, {'abstract': 'Trump’s tweets undermine what I thought it meant to participate in American democracy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/31/opinion/trump-baltimore.html', 'snippet': 'Trump’s tweets undermine what I thought it meant to participate in American democracy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — I walked into the United States Citizenship and Immigration Services branch here on a hot afternoon two weeks ago. After passing through security, I entered a waiting room that looked like your average D.M.V. The majority of the people looked like me in that they were people of color, and they had come from a different part of the world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multi