irstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47db6fe5-2df4-586d-a132-7504c21572f2', 'word_count': 805, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47db6fe5-2df4-586d-a132-7504c21572f2'}, {'abstract': 'Eight Republican House members have announced their retirement this year, with more predicted to follow. What’s going on?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/07/31/opinion/republicans-congress.html', 'snippet': 'Eight Republican House members have announced their retirement this year, with more predicted to follow. What’s going on?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday afternoon, Representative Mike Conaway, Republican of Texas, announced that he would not run for re-election next year. At a news conference in Midland, Mr. Conaway expressed distress at the partisan dysfunction in Congress, nodded to the term limits that his party places on committee leadership positions and said he’d been pondering retirement for a year or so. He said he wanted to leave on his “own terms.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/opinion/31retirements/31retirements-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 721, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/07/31/opinion/31retirements/31retirements-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 721}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/opinion/31retirements/31retirements-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 852, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/07/31/opinion/31retirements/31retir